Licensing of the postgresql/ workload
=====================================

Material derived from PostgreSQL: the injection patches (bugs/*/injection.patch,
patches/), the reproducers (repro.sql, repro.sh, expected_clean.out,
expected_injected.out), and the PostgreSQL test names, code excerpts and commit
messages quoted in oracle.json, meta.json and RATIONALE.md. It is derived from
PostgreSQL's source, test suite and history (https://github.com/postgres/postgres,
release REL_18_6) and is licensed under the PostgreSQL License, below.
Portions Copyright (c) 1996-2026, PostgreSQL Global Development Group;
Portions Copyright (c) 1994, The Regents of the University of California.

Everything else in this directory (the bin/ scripts, tool/, the README,
marauder.toml, bugs.csv, and the labels and verification records in meta.json,
oracle.json and RATIONALE.md) is Copyright Datadog, Inc. and licensed under the
Apache License 2.0 (../LICENSE).

The following is PostgreSQL's COPYRIGHT file at REL_18_6
(https://github.com/postgres/postgres/blob/REL_18_6/COPYRIGHT), verbatim:

